    <string name="cfg_help_encoder">Encoder compresses video to a smaller file. Hardware encoding is faster but slightly lower quality; software encoding has better quality but is slower.</string>
    <string name="cfg_help_bitrate">Bitrate determines video data per second. Higher = better quality but larger file. Recommended: 2-4 Mbps for short clips, 1-2 Mbps for long videos.</string>
    <string name="cfg_help_crf">CRF (Constant Rate Factor) controls quality. 0=lossless, 23=default, 51=worst. Lower value = larger file = better quality.</string>
    <string name="cfg_help_preset">Software encoding preset speed. 9 levels from ultrafast to veryslow; slower = better compression = smaller file.</string>
    <string name="cfg_help_framerate">Frames per second. Original keeps the source; lowering reduces file size but may affect smoothness.</string>
    <string name="cfg_help_resolution">Output resolution. Original keeps the source size; lowering reduces file size significantly.</string>
    <string name="cfg_help_audio">Audio encoder. Copy preserves original audio (fastest); AAC has best compatibility.</string>
    <string name="cfg_help_audio_bitrate">Audio bitrate. Higher = better quality but larger file. 128k is typical.</string>
    <string name="cfg_help_audio_sample_rate">Audio sample rate. Original keeps the source; lowering reduces file size.</string>

